{
  "contract_version": 3,
  "notes": [
    "Capability-negotiated addition to native-v2: every v1/v2 request and response keeps its shape; v3 adds optional fields and two endpoints.",
    "A device is online while it holds a connection lease. A lease is taken when the device actually connects (POST /connections or POST /grants), never by login, catalog reads or selection.",
    "client_reported leases are renewed by POST /traffic; node_reported leases by GET /session while the grant is live. Leases last lease_seconds; a lapsed lease is never renewed.",
    "The session snapshot gains connection_id, connection_state (active, expired or ended) and connection_expires_at, present once the session has held a lease.",
    "Session reasons connection_expired (lease lapsed) and connection_reassigned (server withdrawn; reconnect to the same group) apply to leases taken by v3 calls; an older Core admitted through GET /config is told profile_changed instead.",
    "POST /connections/:id/release is idempotent and only accepts the listed reasons; tunnel_unhealthy and tunnel_failed are recorded as failure reports.",
    "Online devices per user are capped at min(subscription max_devices, server CLIENT_MAX_ONLINE_DEVICES); a device counts once however often it connects.",
    "node_id in POST /grants names the group; a server id from an older client resolves to its group. avoid_node_id excludes one server for a single retry."
  ],
